/// local anisotropy of the sastrugi.\r
///\r
/// One global bearing gives every ridge in the field the same direction and the\r
/// same aspect ratio, and the result reads as corduroy — a woven texture laid\r
/// over the landform rather than snow carved by weather. Real sastrugi does not\r
/// do that: the wind veers as it crosses a dune, so the field breaks into patches\r
