/// Footprint-filtered fine layer, for the fragment shader.\r
///\r
/// Each layer fades out once its wavelength drops near the size of a pixel.\r
/// Without this the sastrugi turns into a crawling moiré carpet across the\r
/// mid-distance the moment the camera moves — and unlike geometry aliasing, TAA\r
/// cannot rescue normal-map aliasing, because the signal is already wrong before\r
/// it is sampled. Fading is not a quality compromise here; it *is* the filter.\r
///\r
/// \`fp\` is the world-space size of one pixel, from fwidth() on world position.\r
