// The snow material.\r
//\r
// Normals arrive from four independent sources and have to be combined in the\r
// right order or the surface stops holding together:\r
//\r
//   macro     baked landform gradient        tens of metres → ~1 m\r
//   fine      analytic sastrugi and ripples  ~2 m → ~10 cm\r
//   detail    tiled generated grain map      ~10 cm → ~5 mm\r
//   deform    the terrain state buffer       whatever the player carved\r
//\r
// Macro and fine and deform are all *heightfield gradients* in world space, so\r
// they add as slopes before ever becoming a normal. Only the detail map is a\r
// tangent-space normal, and it is folded in last with reoriented normal mapping.\r
// Adding normals instead of slopes is the classic way to lose the landform under\r
// the detail.\r
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\r
