        // behind a distance fade. Two texels differenced at 30 m is a normal\r
        // sampled far below the pixel's own footprint, so it aliases. Fading it\r
        // out fixes the aliasing but stops the trail existing about fifteen\r
        // metres out, and a run should be visible from across the field.\r
        //\r
        // Widening the baseline is the better answer: it is the low-pass filter\r
        // the fade was standing in for. The difference stays bounded while the\r
        // divisor grows, so the gradient rolls off smoothly with distance instead\r
