    // version's did not. Fading the range out at a fixed elevation angle drew a\r
    // dead straight horizontal line under the whole massif — a ruler across the\r
    // frame, which is the one thing a landscape never has. A real range's feet are\r
    // hidden by the land in front of it, and here that happens for free: the\r
    // clipmap is drawn *after* the sky and covers everything below its own\r
    // silhouette, so letting the range paint down past the horizon lets the near\r
    // dunes occlude it exactly where they actually stand. A ray at -0.05 from eye\r
    // height meets the ground inside eighty metres, so there is nowhere it can\r
    // escape the terrain and show a base.\r
